{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/984343-big-list-of-generic-human-npcs","id":984343,"title":"Big List of Generic Human NPCs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-09T04:21:46-07:00","id":984343,"title":"Big List of Generic Human NPCs?","content":"Does anyone know if there's a big list of generic human NPCs somewhere handy on the internet?<br /> <br /> Sometimes, rather than either handcrafting an NPC or improvising on the spot I'd like to simple cut and paste some stats from a PDF or website.<br /> <br /> e.g. I have a minor NPC, ordinary human, who's a photographer. I could simply assign 2 to all her stats and relevant skills, maybe 3 dots in Craft (photography) but I'd like to see someone else's take on such a generic character.<br /> <br /> Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:06:28-07:00","id":984378,"title":"","content":"Probably not exactly what you're looking for, but in the past, whenever I've used such a thing, I've always ended up having to make the character more real because I ended up involving them much, much more than I had initially thought I would. I like to make everything in my games connect to itself and to a central theme, so when I've eventually needed a character who's the niece of the X or who will take over the business from Y, it's been the previously generic character that the PCs spoke to for five minutes and for some reason really liked. So I've stopped using those sorts of generic characters and I just make them complex real people from the beginning, since I have to end up making them complex with backstories eventually anyway. Just a thought, I know it's not what you were looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T10:39:02-07:00","id":985501,"title":"","content":"I agree this would be a great resource, but I can't help you unfortunately. If I'm making an NPC in advance that I know I'm going to use, I give them full stats like hm8453a, and if it's someone who I have to make up on the spot, I make their stats up on the spot, too (by default, 4-5 dice in whatever skills they use day-to-day, 2 in all virtues, Willpower 4-5 and 1-3 dice in anything else. It's rarely relevant to know such a character's Backgrounds.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T15:59:18-07:00","id":987479,"title":"","content":"I think I'm just gonna have to agree with the two posters above me: after all, there's really no such thing as a truly &quot;generic&quot; person.<br /> <br /> Everybody's got their own unique hopes, dreams, aspirations - no matter how plain their aspect or bland their voice, the soul is seldom composed entire of such dull, flat hues.<br /> <br /> Lurking <i>somewhere</i> in the back of the mind of that terribly unremarkable &quot;Photographer #4&quot; NPC you have there is likely to be at least <i>one</i> remarkable thought - the best advice I can give to you would be to figure out what that thought is, and build from there. Your players will probably thank you for the depth.<br /> <br /> Remember, also, that every character's stats can tell a story: with your photographer, are they good? Mediocre? Desperately talented, or just desperate? From those four vague ideas alone, we could justify Crafts (Photography) dots totals of one to four, and how talented you decide they are (and how honest you decide they are <i>about</i> that talent) will influence every interaction they have with the PCs, and thereby how the players are likely to respond to her.<br /> <br /> That'd be my take, anyway. Maybe it'll serve you some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:47:20-07:00","id":987561,"title":"","content":"I can share ye one of my NPC's i used on my DtF game<br /> Lincoln Stavros: Serbian cab driver trying to live the american dream. he is very polite, always caring, he will always try to help everyone around him (even if that costs him a lot). i partially based him on Cousin Roman (GTA IV) and in Ranjit (How i Meet your Mother)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:33:48-07:00","id":987623,"title":"","content":"I have a notebook somewhere with around 100 NPCs that I alter as needed to fit my games. Here is an example.<br /> <br /> Tasha Raven Feather (Bartender)<br /> <br /> Tasha is a woman of rare virtue. She is generous of spirit and strong of will but, despite her exceptional nature, she has only ended up as a bartender in a corner bar. While she makes enough money to cover her bills, she is disappointed that she has not been able to do more with her life.<br /> <br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Appearance 3<br /> Perception 2, Intelligence 3, Wits 2<br /> <br /> Alertness 1, Athletics 1, Awareness 1, Brawl 1, Empathy 1, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 1<br /> Animal Ken 1, Bartender 3, Drive 1, Etiquette 1, Firearms 1, Melee 1, Performance 1, Stealth 1, Survival 1<br /> Computer 1, Medicine 1, Occult 1, Technology 1<br /> <br /> Allies 3, Contacts 3, Resources 1<br /> <br /> Conscience 5, Courage 5, Self-Control 4<br /> <br /> Humanity 9<br /> <br /> Willpower 10<br /> <br /> True Faith 1<br /> <br /> Alternate (No Humanity/Virtues): Dexterity+1, Stamina+1, Allies-2.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 10-15-2016, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:16:54-07:00","id":987784,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm just going to have to build up the same sort of notebook. I was kind of hoping that someone else would already have published theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}